  "summary": "ReversingLabs profiles three actively maintained infostealer malware-as-a-service families active between June and August 2026: AuraStealer (now virtualized and 10MB in size), ACRStealer/Amatera, and Remus Stealer, a 64-bit LummaStealer-like stealer that uniquely uses Etherhiding for C2. All three harvest browser credentials and crypto wallet data, rely on heavy anti-analysis and self-deletion, and are distributed through ClickFix, ClearFake, SEO poisoning and malvertising. The report provides hashes, download URLs and C2 domains for each family.",
